[00:00.00]All right, class, let's dive into this fun translation activity together. Today, we're looking at sentences in Portuguese, and our job is to translate them into English. This will not only help us practice our language skills, but also understand everyday phrases that could be useful in day-to-day conversations. Let's begin with sentence number one. Eu bebo café com leite de manhã. This translates to, I drink coffee with milk in the morning. Notice how manhã means morning, and café com leite is coffee with milk. Moving on to number two. Você bebe chá no café da manhã? Translates to, do you drink tea at breakfast? Here, chá is tea, which is a great word to remember, especially if you enjoy a warm cup in the morning or any time of day. Now let's look at number three. Eu quero comer pão com queijo todos os dias. This means, I want to eat bread with cheese every day. Pão com queijo is bread with cheese, a delicious and simple combo. For sentence four, você come uma maçã e bebe suco de laranja de tarde. We translate it to, you eat an apple and drink orange juice in the afternoon. Maçã is apple, and suco de laranja is orange juice. Let's pick one more to practice translation. Sentence seven is, você quer comer comida mexicana no jantar? Which translates to, do you want to eat Mexican food for dinner? Comida mexicana means Mexican food, and jantar is dinner. Keep practicing these translations at home and try making up your own sentences using these structures. The more you practice, the more comfortable you'll become with the language. Happy learning!